# Keep the essential desktop toolbar visible
Workstream-ID: lea-21
GitHub-Issue: https://github.com/Zanark/LinkedIn-EasyApply-Automaton/issues/21

Status: DONE
Milestone: Prevent accidental hiding of configuration and help controls
Dependencies: None
Publication: PUBLIC_SAFE_PROJECTION

## Purpose
Remove the native toolbar visibility menu that can hide the only top toolbar
when its Main checkbox is unchecked.

## Tasks
- Reproduce the context-menu event path in an isolated offscreen window.
- Disable the default main-window visibility popup, preserving text editing.
- Check tutorial access, reopening and unchanged saved configuration/preferences.
- Update affected guides and reconcile only this workstream's tracking.

## Acceptance criteria
- Right-clicking Tutorial or the toolbar cannot offer a Main hide checkbox.
- Text-field context menus and existing Tutorial/F1 behavior remain available.
- Reopening restores an older hidden toolbar without resetting the setup.
- Checks use fictional temporary state and do not control an existing instance.
- Technical verification is distinct from native acceptance and publication.

## Completion evidence
Local implementation and bounded offline verification are complete.
An actual context-menu event reproduced the native Main visibility action
before the fix. MainWindow now returns no default toolbar popup; both themes
cover right-clicks on Tutorial and the toolbar, normal configuration-field
editing menus, and reopening an older hidden bar without resetting saved
configuration, answers or theme.

All 167 cases across the five GUI suites passed with native exit zero,
including eight focused new cases. Black/Ruff passed the two changed Python
files; mypy passed all ten GUI source files. Seven affected guides are updated.
The normal visible layout and all existing media remain unchanged.

Checks use temporary fictional workspaces and isolated INI preferences.
No existing user process is inspected, stopped or restarted. Source changes
remain local and uncommitted; released v0.2.1 is unchanged. Offline checks are
not installed-release qualification, live automation or human acceptance.
Scoped issue/Project/backlink settlement is recorded separately.

## Completion log
- 2026-11-10: Removed the accidental visibility menu while preserving native
  field editing, Tutorial/F1 behavior and existing configuration/preferences.
  GUI regressions and scoped static checks pass; recovery requires only a
  manual reopen after the current run and unsaved edits are handled.
- 2026-11-10: The first tracking preview rejected a missing Publication field
  without remote writes. Corrected the reviewed publication declaration;
  the subsequent scoped preview passed without weakening validation.
- 2026-11-10: Started a bounded desktop-only fix. Preserve prior source work,
  configuration, history, existing releases and independently opened instances.
